//! crunk's rule crate (D107, `rule-authoring.md`; design `crunk.md` section 6): the families crunk
//! owns, the registry over every `#[rule]` declaration, the `[lint]` severity resolution and the
//! `crunk:waive` waivers with their one rule, WAIVE001.
//!
//! # Overview
//!
//! - [`rules`]: one `src/rules/<id>.rs` plus `<id>.md` per rule, the index generated by
//!   `cargo dev gen rules-index`. WAIVE001, COLOR001-002, CONTRAST001, LAYER001, ORG001-005, TW001-005, BP001-003 and TOKENS001 live here; later crunk
//!   rules join the same directory (or another crate listed in `crunk-check`'s `product_rules!`).
//! - [`color`], [`contrast`], [`mode`], [`sheets`]: the plain modules the colour and contrast rules
//!   share (palette conformance, the definition set, role measurement, the mode loop, site paths).
//! - [`family`]: [`family::FamilyMeta`], the metadata a family shares (tiers, waivability and the
//!   release severity room), and [`family::Gate`] with [`family::gate_severity`].
//! - [`registry`]: [`registry::entries`] lists id, family, default severity, fixable flag and doc
//!   of every declared rule; [`registry::render_markdown`] is the generated page under
//!   `docs/crunk/rules/`.
//! - [`lint`]: `[lint]` of `crunk.toml` applied to a declared rule or to a finding.
//! - [`waiver`]: the `crunk:waive` comment: scan, bind to the covered region, turn into exceptions.
//! - [`layers`], [`org`]: what LAYER001 and ORG001-005 share (declared z-index values, ignore globs,
//!   class casing and component prefixes).
//! - [`tailwind`], [`breakpoints`]: what TW001-005 and BP001-003 share (arbitrary-value splitting,
//!   the scale judgment, the `tw_theme` view, breakpoint tolerance and base families). TOKENS001
//!   compares [`GeneratedFile`] (from `crunk-tokens`) with the bytes on disk.
//! - [`host`]: [`host::CrunkHost`], the host trait crunk's rules evaluate against.

